From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <jpm820@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:39:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] NextBSD: loader under U-Boot, the screen is the console

U-Boot's EFI sets no ConOut, ConOutDev or ConIn variable, so
parse_uefi_con_out() takes its "no Con* variable" branch on every
U-Boot boot and asks for both consoles: console="efi,comconsole" and
RB_MULTIPLE. Both turn boot-video graphics mode off, in the loader
(patch 0011 needs no serial port in ConOut) and in the kernel, which
reads comconsole in the console variable as a serial-console request.
On a Raspberry Pi 500+ booted through U-Boot (nextbsd/nextbsd#687) the
boot was therefore always text: no splash and no spinner.

When the firmware is U-Boot and there is a GOP, use the screen only,
console="efi", as ConOut would say on other firmware. Other firmware,
and U-Boot with no display, keep the stock behaviour. A serial console
is still one loader.conf line away (console="efi,comconsole" or
boot_serial), and either one leaves graphics mode.

CI's OVMF and AAVMF set ConOut and never reach this branch.

Part of nextbsd/nextbsd#542 (nextbsd-freebsd-compat#88).

Carried out-of-tree for NextBSD.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 stand/efi/loader/main.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/stand/efi/loader/main.c b/stand/efi/loader/main.c
index d119c3116..e765ccde0 100644
--- a/stand/efi/loader/main.c
+++ b/stand/efi/loader/main.c
@@ -1049,6 +1049,17 @@ check_acpi_spcr(void)
 	return (RB_SERIAL);
 }
 
+/* NextBSD: U-Boot's EFI ("Das U-Boot", lib/efi_loader/efi_boottime.c). */
+static bool
+efi_firmware_is_uboot(void)
+{
+	char vendor[32];
+
+	if (ST->FirmwareVendor == NULL)
+		return (false);
+	cpy16to8(ST->FirmwareVendor, vendor, sizeof(vendor));
+	return (strcmp(vendor, "Das U-Boot") == 0);
+}
 
 /*
  * Parse ConOut (the list of consoles active) and see if we can find a serial
@@ -1091,7 +1102,19 @@ parse_uefi_con_out(void)
 		 * omit this, but has a serial port redirect, we'll unavoidably
 		 * get doubled characters, but we'll be right in all the other
 		 * more common cases.
+		 *
+		 * NextBSD: U-Boot never sets a Con* variable, so on U-Boot
+		 * this branch is every boot, and the serial half turns
+		 * boot-video graphics mode off in both the loader and the
+		 * kernel.  With a GOP, U-Boot's screen is the console, as
+		 * ConOut would say on any other firmware.  loader.conf's
+		 * console="efi,comconsole" (or boot_serial) still asks for
+		 * serial, and leaves graphics mode.
 		 */
+		if (efi_has_gop() && efi_firmware_is_uboot()) {
+			setenv("console", "efi", 1);
+			goto out;
+		}
 		if (efi_has_gop())
 			how |= RB_MULTIPLE;
 		else
-- 
